#! ia 1.0

@capability kb-knowledge
  meaning
    says "Work in the KB lane: where a spec, PRD, policy or decision lives (organisation KB or source repository) and where a workspace is saved, binding a @spec anchor to its body, keeping KB documents current, migrating a knowledge workspace, and checking and reviewing a KB. The entry capability the core's Knowledge entry point binds, and a whole procedure: its kb-knowledge playbook orients, plans, acts and learns for any knowledge request, choosing the stage, naming the roles and handing native application to the Delivery lane. It includes one capability per stage and the retrieval and review capabilities. It installs reusable expertise, not an organisation's corpus or access grants, and it grants no authority; the workspace's mandates and the human's word decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which capability does an agent bind for KB placement, workspace location, binding, maintenance, migration, checks and review?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook kb-knowledge]
    includes [@capability kb-place-content, @capability kb-bind-document, @capability kb-maintain-document, @capability kb-check, @capability kb-migrate, @capability kb-retrieve, @capability kb-review]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@capability kb-place-content
  meaning
    says "Place a spec, PRD, policy or decision in its authoritative KB or source repository, and a workspace in its location: identify purpose, accountable owner, audience, change coupling, canonical body and existing native identity, recommend the smallest durable placement, save a user's workspace under ~/Documents/ia/<name> unless they name another location and never inside ~/.ia, list the affected links, locators and access paths, and return the placement, rationale, binding and any unresolved ownership choice. Use for where a document or a workspace should live."
    answers "Where should this document live?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook kb-place-content]
  execution
    effects [read]

@capability kb-bind-document
  meaning
    says "Bind a @spec anchor to one exact document body (repository, commit, path, sha256): preserve the document ID, native spec identity, repository identity, exact commit, repo-relative path and byte digest, use an ordinary relative work.source for a local body and a revision-pinned repo:// locator with a companion ia.document-locators.v1 manifest for a body in another repository, keep lifecycle decisions and body disclosure separate, verify bytes by running the kit's locator checker directly on the task's manifest with --checkout when that is authorized, and report metadata-only checks apart from verified bytes. Use when work.source must point at a specific body."
    answers "How is a @spec anchor bound to one exact document body?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook kb-bind-document]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@capability kb-maintain-document
  meaning
    says "Add or revise KB documents with their @spec records and navigation: select the canonical corpus and authorized writer, create the body and exactly one canonical @spec anchor or preserve identity on a revision, keep frontmatter consistent with the anchor, update the corpus index and navigation, keep a made or superseded @decision's acceptance and a superseded one's successor (the declared check kb-check-decisions), preserve any existing guard, and run the checks through kb-check. Use for adding a document to the KB or updating a decision."
    answers "How is a KB document added or revised with its anchor and navigation?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook kb-maintain-document]
    checks [@check kb-check-validate, @check kb-check-decisions]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@capability kb-check
  meaning
    says "Check a KB: record admission, document-to-spec coverage, the decision lifecycle, navigation and kit evaluator results, without conflating not-evaluated with pass. Run ia position for the task scope, then ia validate (the declared check kb-check-validate, which the kb-gate-runner can run) and the decision lifecycle (the declared check kb-check-decisions: a made @decision names its decider, choice and rationale, and a superseded one keeps them and has a successor; the accepted revision is not required yet), the KB's own index and check workflow and tests when it supplies them, and report the revision, tool provenance, checks run, passed, failed and not-evaluated requirements and missing evaluators. Use for checking the KB or after KB maintenance."
    answers "Does this KB admit, cover its documents and keep its navigation current?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook kb-check]
    checks [@check kb-check-validate, @check kb-check-decisions]
  execution
    effects [read]

@capability kb-migrate
  meaning
    says "Migrate a legacy IA knowledge workspace to the three-record IA starter in an isolated copy: record the provenance, confirm the installed CLI supports migration, restore and validate the baseline, preview ia init <root> --migrate, apply only a conflict-free plan, preserve a multi-system provider workspace and any existing guard, and compare identities, locators, navigation and host projection before and after. Use when ia init --migrate is involved."
    answers "How is a legacy knowledge workspace migrated to the three-record IA starter?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook kb-migrate]
    checks [@check kb-check-validate]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@capability kb-retrieve
  meaning
    says "Retrieve bounded KB context with canonical anchors and source attribution: record IDs, revisions, and the bodies the audience may read, through ia position and the KB's own find and context tools when it supplies them, distinguishing unavailable or stale bodies. Read-only. The kb-librarian's capability; use to locate information or have it explained from its sources."
    answers "What does the KB hold on this question, and from which records and revisions?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook kb-retrieval]
  execution
    effects [read]

@capability kb-review
  meaning
    says "Review KB document changes, lifecycle evidence or maintenance check results independently before acceptance: read the exact candidate and source evidence, check identity, lifecycle decision authority, scope, references and reported evaluator results, and return actionable findings with evidence. Read-only, never on work the reviewer authored. The kb-reviewer's capability."
    answers "Is this KB change ready for acceptance, and what is wrong with it?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook kb-review]
  execution
    effects [read]

@capability kb-gates
  meaning
    says "Run the KB kit's four declared checks through the core's checker runner, each by its fixed command, and report the command, exit code and output verbatim: kb-check-validate (ia validate --json in the workspace under check), kb-check-decisions (the kit's decision checker over the workspace's admitted records), kb-check-locators (the kit's locator checker over the kit's own worked example, metadata only) and kb-check-task-locators (the same checker over a task's own manifest). The kb-gate-runner's capability: kb-check delegates its declared gates to it. For a task manifest, run kb-check-task-locators with --manifest naming a workspace-relative regular file. This check reports metadata-only standing and never substitutes the example. It runs nothing else."
    answers "Do the KB kit's declared checks pass on this host and workspace?"
  composition
    checks [@check kb-check-validate, @check kb-check-locators, @check kb-check-task-locators, @check kb-check-decisions]
  execution
    effects [read]
